cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this design or code, please cite it as below."
title: "Star tracker: an ESP32 barn-door tracker with firmware tangent correction"
authors:
  - family-names: Kronbi
    given-names: Rami
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A 3D-printed barn-door star tracker for DSLR astrophotography. ESP32 firmware schedules each
  microstep from the closed-form inverse of the mechanism's geometry; a Python tracking-error
  model predicts the longest sharp exposure; a planner finds moonless M42 windows from Beirut.
  Hardware design under CERN-OHL-P-2.0; code under MIT. Performance figures are predictions.
keywords:
  - astrophotography
  - star tracker
  - barn door
  - ESP32
  - embedded
  - OpenSCAD
